# Genus does not increase under algebraically closed constant field extension

Theorem statement: `AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_le_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`
(`90cf01c5-1813-5cdd-8060-f05695a4ba29`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `8e049f4f-7be9-549b-afe2-0404d97907c2`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K, F, K', F'$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra, $K'$ and $F'$ algebras
over $K$ and $F$ respectively, arranged in compatible towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$,
and assume $K$ and $K'$ are algebraically closed. Assume that $F$ contains an element $x$
transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x)$, and likewise that $F'$ contains an
element transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite over the subfield it generates; so $F/K$ and
$F'/K'$ are function fields of one variable. Assume further that each of $F/K$ and $F'/K'$ satisfies
`IsCurveOver`: every nonzero element has an associated divisor of degree $0$ recording its orders at
all places (a place being a proper valuation subring containing the image of the constant field and
which is a principal ideal ring), every place has residue field finite-dimensional over the constant
field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the function field. Assume
finally that the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$. Then $\dim_{K'}
H^1(0) \le \dim_K H^1(0)$, i.e. `genusFF K' F' ≤ genusFF K F` for the repartition genus.

This is one inequality of the classical statement that the genus of a one-variable function field is
unchanged by extension of an algebraically closed constant field. It is used by
[`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`]
(thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed),
which combines it with the opposite inequality.

